---
import HomeLayout from '../../layouts/HomeLayout.astro';
import { beanReviews } from '../../data/bean-reviews';
import '../../styles/review.css';
import '../../styles/beans.css';
import '../../styles/bean-guides.css';

const date = '2026-10-22';
const path = '/coffee-beans/best-coffee-beans-for-cold-brew/';
const canonical = 'https://coffeedant.com' + path;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const local = (value:string) => base + value.replace(/^\//, '');
const title = 'Best Coffee Beans for Cold Brew at Home';
const description = 'Research-led US whole-bean cold-brew guide: two currently defensible first bags, a fruit-led and a dark-with-milk route, plus stock cautions and a repeatable buying method.';
const specs = [
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/blue-bottle-three-africas/',best:'Fruit-led black cold brew',roast:'Medium',reason:'Blue Bottle explicitly describes this blend cold-brewed and names washed and natural Ethiopian components with a 2026 Rwandan component.',tradeoff:'A new bag may rotate lots; the fruit notes are a roaster target, not our tasting.',skip:'You want a cocoa-only concentrate for a large milk drink.'},
  {slug:'/coffee-beans/blue-bottle-giant-steps/',best:'Dark cold brew with milk',roast:'Dark',reason:'Blue Bottle includes Giant Steps in its cold-brew collection; its product review documents a dark cocoa, toasted-marshmallow and graham-cracker brief.',tradeoff:'Complete current origins and processing are undisclosed; its 1:13 French-press-with-milk ratio is not a cold-brew recipe.',skip:'You want berry, citrus or a clearly named current farm.'}
];
const picks = specs.map(spec=>({...spec,review:beanReviews.find(r=>r.slug===spec.slug)!}));
if(picks.some(p=>!p.review)) throw new Error('Cold-brew guide references a missing full review');
const sections = [
  {id:'method',title:'Why the shortlist is deliberately small',paragraphs:[
    'Cold brew is a brewing method, not a roast category. A coarse grind steeps in cool water for hours before filtering; the bean still determines the roaster’s flavor target. We looked for exact US whole-bean identity, a current official cold-brew recommendation or collection placement, a distinct buyer job, a linked full review and a material reason to skip. Blue Bottle Three Africas and Giant Steps meet those criteria as two different first-bag decisions. [1] [2] [3]',
    'We screened Peet’s Baridi Blend, Off the Grid, Big Bang and Sun Catcher because Peet’s marks cold-brew roles for those coffees. The current official product pages for these exact bags displayed sold-out notices at this check. They remain useful comparisons in their linked reviews but are not active buy-now picks. A web listing with a price beside “sold out” is not an offer. [4] [5] [6] [7]',
    'The best-for labels below are research-led judgments about fit, documentation and availability. Coffeedant has not bought or tasted these bags or run controlled extraction tests. Only the delivered roast date, the selected whole-bean variant and a repeatable home steep can settle an individual household choice.'
  ]},
  {id:'brew-method',title:'Start with one measured steep',paragraphs:[
    'Use a coarse grind, weighed coffee and water, a clean food-safe vessel and a complete filtration step. Stumptown’s cold-brew guidance describes 12–24 hours as a broad route; Peet’s product panels use 12-plus hours. Neither is a promise that one fixed time suits every bean, vessel, grind and refrigerator. Record the water temperature, time and concentrate dilution before judging a second bag. [8] [4]',
    'A cold-steep concentrate and a ready-to-drink cold brew are different ratios. If you add ice or milk, write down that serving dilution too. A stronger steep can taste weak after heavy dilution, while a fine grind or poor filtration can make any bean seem muddy. Change one variable at a time; do not copy Giant Steps’ French-press-with-milk 1:13 figure into a cold-brew recipe. [2]',
    'Filter and refrigerate the finished drink promptly according to the brewing equipment’s food-safety guidance. The long steep is not an excuse to leave an opened bag in heat or sunlight. Grind only what the batch needs and check the actual roast date when the whole beans arrive. [8] [9]'
  ]},
  {id:'flavor',title:'Choose the chilled cup before the brand',paragraphs:[
    'Three Africas is the fruit-led path. Blue Bottle names golden raisin, winey blueberry and lemon zest and says its washed and natural Ethiopian components and Central African coffee make a cold-brewed blend with depth. These are attributed descriptions, not tasting notes from Coffeedant. If you drink black cold brew, its intended fruit direction is easier to test without milk. [1]',
    'Giant Steps is the dark, milk-oriented path. Blue Bottle lists cocoa, toasted marshmallow and graham cracker and places it in the cold-brew collection. The roaster also gives a separate French-press-with-milk suggestion. We infer it is a more natural starting point for a milk-diluted dark cup; that inference is not a measured claim that it beats Three Africas in any recipe. [2] [3]',
    'Roast darkness alone cannot rank cold brew. Blue Bottle’s two bags differ in declared components, flavor direction and intended presentation. Try one small bag, keep preparation consistent, and let the chilled, filtered cup decide whether to repeat it or switch.'
  ]},
  {id:'availability',title:'What to do when the purpose-built bag is sold out',paragraphs:[
    'Peet’s Baridi has the strongest café identity: Peet’s says it uses the blend for coffeebar cold brew. The official US bean page nevertheless showed sold out. Do not substitute a ready-to-drink Baridi beverage or an unrelated shop that resembles Peet’s official domain. Save its full review and recheck legitimate whole-bean stock and roast date later. [4]',
    'Off the Grid, Big Bang and Sun Catcher also appeared in Peet’s cold-brew collection, but their product pages displayed sold-out notices at this check. Off the Grid’s washed Colombia-and-El Salvador profile is a chocolate-and-pear alternative; Big Bang is medium and fruit-tart; Sun Catcher is a bright Brazil-and-Kenya, pour-over-first coffee with cold brew as another method. Their official method labels do not override missing live stock. [5] [6] [7]',
    'If a legitimate seller has one of these exact bags, compare the live whole-bean size, roast date, shipping and tax with the two first picks. A lower price on a different grind, old stock or subscription schedule cannot establish a better current value.'
  ]},
  {id:'freshness',title:'Buy the amount you will actually brew',paragraphs:[
    'A 12 oz bag is about 340 g. At 30 g per batch it provides roughly eleven theoretical batches before grinder loss; concentrate recipes can consume more. Those are arithmetic illustrations, not Coffeedant recipes or serving-size promises. Start with one bag and calculate from your actual dose, dilution and drinking frequency. [1] [2]',
    'Keep opened whole beans sealed in a cool, dry place away from odors and grind before steeping. Blue Bottle product photographs identify the current brand and bag but cannot certify the delivered roast date or time in transit. A recurring blend may rotate components while holding a similar flavor target. [1] [9]',
    'No numeric one-time delivered US price is ranked here because exact selector, shipping, tax and active stock were not verified on the same basis across all candidates. Use check-price links and the current cart rather than a stale list price.'
  ]}
];
const faqs = [
  {q:'Which whole bean should I try first for black cold brew?',a:'Blue Bottle Three Africas has an explicit cold-brew description and a fruit-led roaster brief. Start with one bag and a consistent steep; Coffeedant has not tasted it.'},
  {q:'Which pick is better with milk?',a:'Giant Steps is our research-led dark-with-milk start because of its cocoa-led brief. Its published French-press ratio is not a cold-brew ratio.'},
  {q:'Why is Peet’s Baridi not a current pick?',a:'The official US whole-bean page displayed a sold-out notice on October 22, 2026. Its café cold-brew role is well documented, but current purchase availability was not established.'},
  {q:'Must cold-brew beans be dark?',a:'No. Three Africas is medium and fruit-led. Choose the flavor direction and method evidence that match the intended chilled cup.'},
  {q:'Can I reuse a French-press recipe?',a:'Keep the device-specific grind, immersion time, filtration and serving dilution separate. A hot French-press ratio does not automatically transfer to a cold steep.'},
  {q:'Are the flavors or prices Coffeedant measurements?',a:'No. Flavor words are attributed to the roasters. No comparative sensory score or current delivered price ranking is asserted.'},
  {q:'How do I compare two bags fairly?',a:'Use the same grinder, coarse setting, dose, water, vessel, steep conditions, filter and serving dilution. Note the roast dates of the actual delivered bags.'}
];
const sources = [
  ['Blue Bottle US: Three Africas','https://bluebottlecoffee.com/us/eng/product/three-africas','Current blend identity and cold-brewed positioning.'],
  ['Blue Bottle US: Giant Steps','https://bluebottlecoffee.com/us/eng/product/giant-steps','Dark-roast flavor brief and separate press guidance.'],
  ['Blue Bottle: cold-brew collection','https://bluebottlecoffee.com/us/eng/collection/cold-brew','Current collection placement for both selected blends.'],
  ["Peet’s US: Baridi Blend",'https://www.peets.com/products/baridi-blend','Café cold-brew identity and sold-out notice.'],
  ["Peet’s US: Off the Grid",'https://www.peets.com/products/off-the-grid','Washed two-country blend and sold-out notice.'],
  ["Peet’s US: Big Bang",'https://www.peets.com/products/big-bang','Medium-roast cold-brew role and sold-out notice.'],
  ["Peet’s US: Sun Catcher",'https://www.peets.com/products/suncatcher','Pour-over-first bright blend, cold-brew option and sold-out notice.'],
  ['Stumptown: cold-brew guidance','https://www.stumptowncoffee.com/collections/cold-brew','Broad coarse-grind and steep method; not a product-specific recipe.'],
  ['Stumptown: whole-bean storage','https://support.stumptowncoffee.com/hc/en-us/articles/5568076789901-Where-should-I-store-my-coffee-In-the-freezer-On-the-counter','Opened-bean storage context.']
];
const cite=(p:string)=>p.replace(/\[(\d+)\]/g,(_m,n)=>'<a class="bean-cite" href="#s'+n+'" aria-label="Source '+n+'">['+n+']</a>');
const author={'@type':'Person',name:'Aleksandar Spasevski',jobTitle:'Editor, Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/about/',image:'https://coffeedant.com/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg'};
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@graph':[
  {'@type':'Article','@id':canonical+'#article',headline:title,description,genre:'Research-led coffee buying guide',inLanguage:'en-US',datePublished:date,dateModified:date,author,mainEntityOfPage:canonical,image:picks.map(p=>p.review.image),citation:sources.map(s=>s[1]),publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/'}},
  {'@type':'ItemList','@id':canonical+'#shortlist',name:title,itemListElement:picks.map((p,i)=>({'@type':'ListItem',position:i+1,name:p.review.roaster+' '+p.review.coffee,url:'https://coffeedant.com'+p.slug}))},
  {'@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:'https://coffeedant.com/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'Coffee beans',item:'https://coffeedant.com/coffee-beans/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:3,name:title,item:canonical}]},
  {'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faqs.map(f=>({'@type':'Question',name:f.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:f.a}}))}
]};
---
<HomeLayout title={title+' | Coffeedant'} description={description} canonicalPath={path} image={picks[0].review.image} imageAlt={picks[0].review.imageAlt} ogType="article" published={date} updated={date}>
  <main id="main-content" class="review-page bean-buying-guide" data-guide-kind="coffee-beans">
    <div class="review-shell">
      <nav class="review-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Home</a><span>/</span><a href={local('/coffee-beans/')}>Coffee beans</a><span>/</span><span>Cold brew</span></nav>
      <header class="bean-guide-header"><p class="review-overline">Coffee buying guide · research-led · United States</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="bean-lead">Start with the chilled cup: fruit-led black coffee or a darker concentrate for milk. Two whole-bean picks have distinct evidence; current sold-out alternatives are clearly separated.</p><aside class="review-author-card"><div class="review-author-head"><img src={local('/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg')} alt="Aleksandar Spasevski, editor at Coffeedant" width="46" height="46" /><div><strong>Aleksandar Spasevski</strong><small>Editor, Coffeedant</small></div></div><p>Published and checked <time datetime={date}>October 22, 2026</time> · US whole-bean context</p><p>I checked current roaster product and method pages, availability notices and linked full reviews. I have not bought, brewed or tasted these coffees. Best-for labels are research-led buying judgments.</p></aside></header>
      <nav class="bean-jump" aria-label="Guide sections"><strong>Choose your cold-brew bean</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={'#'+s.id}>{s.title}</a>)}<a href="#quick-compare">Quick comparison</a><a href="#picks">The picks</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
      <article class="bean-article">
        {sections.slice(0,2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">The buyer decision</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="quick-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Two different cold-brew jobs</p><h2>Quick comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable cold-brew bean comparison"><table><caption>Exact US whole beans checked October 22, 2026; verify the active cart</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Coffee</th><th scope="col">Best for</th><th scope="col">Roast</th><th scope="col">Skip if</th></tr></thead><tbody>{picks.map(p=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.roaster} {p.review.coffee}</a></th><td>{p.best}</td><td>{p.roast}</td><td>{p.skip}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="picks"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">A short list with a reason to skip</p><h2>The two first-bag picks</h2></header><div class="bean-index-grid">{picks.map(p=><article class="bean-guide-pick"><img src={p.review.image} alt={p.review.imageAlt} width="360" height="360" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div><p class="review-overline">{p.best}</p><h3><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.roaster} {p.review.coffee}</a></h3><p><strong>Evidence:</strong> {p.reason}</p><p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> {p.tradeoff}</p><p><strong>Skip if:</strong> {p.skip}</p><p class="bean-credit"><a href={p.review.imageSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Image: {p.review.roaster}</a>. {p.review.imageCredit}</p><a class="bean-guide-review-link" href={local(p.slug)}>Read the full review →</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="detailed-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">The decision behind the label</p><h2>Detailed comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable detailed cold-brew comparison"><table><caption>Roaster-attributed roles and limits; no Coffeedant tasting or current price rank</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Factor</th>{picks.map(p=><th scope="col"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.coffee}</a></th>)}</tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Best chilled role</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.best}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Roaster evidence</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.reason}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Roast direction</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.roast}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Main uncertainty</th>{picks.map(p=><td>{p.tradeoff}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">US checkout</th>{picks.map(_p=><td>Verify whole-bean size, stock, shipping and tax</td>)}</tr></tbody></table></div></section>
        {sections.slice(2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Make the next batch useful</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="related"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Related buyer decisions</p><h2>When cold brew is not the only drink</h2></header><div class="bean-alternatives"><a href={local('/coffee-beans/best-coffee-beans-for-french-press/')}><strong>French press beans</strong><span>Compare separate hot-immersion roles and ratios.</span></a><a href={local('/coffee-beans/best-coffee-beans-for-espresso-and-drip/')}><strong>Espresso and drip</strong><span>Choose one bag for two hot brewing routines.</span></a><a href={local('/coffee-beans/peets-baridi-blend/')}><strong>Baridi stock watch</strong><span>Read the exact blend review, including its current sold-out notice.</span></a></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="methodology"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Evidence and limits</p><h2>How this guide was made</h2></header><div class="review-section-body"><p>We matched exact US whole-bean products to current roaster cold-brew descriptions, compared their documented flavor directions and checked whether the official pages showed a usable purchase path. The two picks have linked research-led reviews. Baridi, Off the Grid, Big Bang and Sun Catcher were excluded from the active shortlist because their official pages displayed sold-out notices. No Coffeedant tasting, extraction measurement or shelf-life experiment was performed.</p><p>Roaster flavor words remain attributed claims, and older independent or owner accounts in the full reviews are limited by lot and method. No numeric price ranking is claimed. Recheck active US stock, exact grind, size, tax and shipping before buying.</p></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="faq"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Quick answers</p><h2>Cold-brew bean FAQ</h2></header><div class="bean-faq">{faqs.map(f=><article><h3>{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="sources"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Attributable evidence</p><h2>Sources checked October 22, 2026</h2></header><ol class="review-source-list">{sources.map((s,i)=><li id={'s'+(i+1)}><a href={s[1]} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{s[0]} ↗</a><p>{s[2]} Checked October 22, 2026.</p></li>)}</ol></section>
        <section class="final-verdict"><p class="review-overline">The useful first bag</p><h2>Choose the chilled cup, then control the steep</h2><p>Start with one whole-bean bag, inspect its roast date and record the grind, dose, steep and serving dilution. Recheck active stock before ordering; the delivered cup, not an unverified score, decides whether to repeat it.</p><a class="review-buy-button review-buy-button-dark" href={local('/coffee-beans/')}>Explore all bean reviews →</a></section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')} />
</HomeLayout>
